### Bug / Limitation Found

After testing the AI-generated Flutter feature, I found that the mock API was a limitation because it returns post data instead of actual book data. The response
did not contain an author field, so the author could not be displayed correctly.

### Fix / Improvement

I checked the JSON response and updated the model parsing to safely handle missing fields. I used a default value such as `"Unknown Author"` when the author field is missing.

I also tested the error handling by checking the loading, success, timeout, and empty-response scenarios. The application now shows a proper message instead of a blank screen or crashing.

### Result

The catalogue feature can now safely display the available data and provide meaningful feedback to the user when data cannot be loaded.
